<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Landgraviate of Hesse-Kassel</h1><p class="st-meta">1567 CE – 1803 CE · capital Kassel</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The largest of the Hessian landgraviates, known for hiring out its soldiers to Britain and for the Wilhelmshöhe palace above Kassel.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When Landgrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-i-landgrave-of-hesse">Philip the Magnanimous</a> died in 1567, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/landgraviate-of-hesse">Landgraviate of Hesse</a> was divided among his four sons. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iv-landgrave-of-hesse-kassel">William IV</a>, the eldest, received about half, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a> as capital, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-hesse">Hesse-Kassel</a> later gained the northern part of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marburg">Marburg</a> in 1604.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iv-landgrave-of-hesse-kassel">William IV</a> was a noted astronomer, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-landgrave-of-hesse-kassel">Maurice the Learned</a> adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calvinism">Calvinism</a> and in 1605 built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoneum">Ottoneum</a>, the first permanent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> building in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amalie-elisabeth-of-hanau-munzenberg">Landgravine Amalie Elisabeth</a> held the land together in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>. In the 18th century the landgraves hired out troops to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, including some 17,000 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chatti">Hessians</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American War of Independence</a>, paying for works such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hercules-kassel">Hercules monument</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergpark-wilhelmshohe">Wilhelmshöhe</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1803 Landgrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-i-elector-of-hesse">William IX</a> was made an elector, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-hesse">Hesse-Kassel</a> became the Electorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> absorbed it into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-westphalia">Kingdom of Westphalia</a> in 1807; restored in 1813, the electorate was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1866.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/landgraviate-of-hesse-kassel.jpg" alt="Landgraviate of Hesse-Kassel" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: kgberger · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hessen_KS_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1567 CE – 1803 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kassel</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William IV, Maurice the Learned, Frederick II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Calvinism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hesse-Cassel, Hessen-Kassel</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1685&amp;focus=landgraviate-of-hesse-kassel" aria-label="Landgraviate of Hesse-Kassel on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4895 400 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Landgraviate of Hesse-Kassel lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5215 656L5215 656M5215 656L5229 694M5215 656L5381 440M5215 656L5215 656M5215 656L5204 690M5215 656L5221 669M5